4. Standard strings of the Compact Font Format

Source: Adobe Technical Note #5176, "The Compact Font Format
Specification", Appendix A, as published in
https://github.com/adobe-type-tools/font-tech-notes (pdfs/5176.CFF.pdf),
under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 International
licence.
Used for: internal/font/cffstrings_gen.go: the glyph name each of the
391 standard string IDs stands for, which reading a CFF font program
requires. Only that list of names is taken, as data; no text of the
document is in this module.

